LIB_LOAD("hw",{"hw1":{"challenge":[{"q":"Who wrote The Holy War?","o":["John Bunyan","Charles Sheldon","C. H. Spurgeon","Mary Slessor"],"why":"The same man who wrote The Pilgrim's Progress, in 1682."},{"q":"Who built Mansoul?","o":["Shaddai, the great King","Diabolus","Lord Willbewill","The people themselves"],"why":"Shaddai means God Almighty."},{"q":"How many gates did Mansoul have?","o":["Five","Two","Seven","Twelve"],"why":"Ear-gate, Eye-gate, Mouth-gate, Nose-gate and Feel-gate."},{"q":"Why was Diabolus thrown out of the King's court?","o":["He grew proud and wanted the King's throne","He was lazy","He stole bread","He was late"],"why":"Pride came before his fall."},{"q":"Who was killed first, before Ill-pause's speech?","o":["Captain Resistance","Mr Conscience","Lord Willbewill","Diabolus"],"why":"Temptation takes out resistance first."},{"q":"Who fell down dead while Ill-pause was speaking?","o":["Lord Innocency","Lord Understanding","Mr Lustings","Mr Forget-good"],"why":"Something in that smooth speech was poison."},{"q":"What happened to Lord Understanding's house?","o":["A wall was built to block its light","It was painted gold","It became a castle","It was given to Mr Conscience"],"why":"Sin darkens the mind."},{"q":"Which lord gladly joined Diabolus?","o":["Lord Willbewill","Lord Innocency","Lord Understanding","Captain Resistance"],"why":"The will chose to serve the enemy."},{"q":"What were Diabolus's three strongholds?","o":["Defiance, Midnight-hold and Sweet-sin-hold","Ear, Eye and Mouth","Hope, Joy and Peace","Gold, Silver and Bronze"],"why":"Places where bad habits dig in."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it are the ___ of life.\"","o":["issues","rivers","secrets","dreams"],"why":"Proverbs 4:23."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Complete the sentence: Diabolus didn't break the gates. He talked the people into ___ them.","o":["opening","painting","selling","locking"],"why":"Temptation works by persuasion, not force."},"choices":[{"title":"The video in the group chat","q":"Someone in your class WhatsApp group posts a video link: \"You people MUST watch this!\" The preview already looks rude and violent.","o":[{"t":"Don't open it. Mute the group, and if it's harmful, tell a parent or teacher.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You kept Eye-gate shut. It's always easier to not look than to forget what you've seen."},{"t":"Leave the group quietly, and suggest a cleaner group to your real friends.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Sometimes guarding your gate means changing where you stand."},{"t":"Open it just to see what everyone is talking about.","f":"That's the 'ill pause': stopping to look when you should walk away."},{"t":"Forward it to another group. You didn't make it.","f":"Now you're opening other people's gates too."}]},{"title":"Gist about a classmate","q":"At break time, your friends start gossiping about a girl in your class, saying cruel things that may not even be true.","o":[{"t":"Change the topic, or kindly say, \"Let's not talk about her like that.\"","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You guarded your Ear-gate and your Mouth-gate, and protected someone else."},{"t":"Just listen quietly. You're not saying anything.","f":"Listening is still letting it in through Ear-gate. Ill-pause loves a quiet audience."},{"t":"Add some gist of your own so you fit in.","f":"Now Mouth-gate is open too."}]},{"title":"Just one taste","q":"At a party, an older cousin hands you a Fanta bottle. You smell it: it's alcohol. \"Just taste small. Nobody will know.\"","o":[{"t":"Say \"No, thanks,\" hand it back, and get a real drink.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You decided before the moment came, like keeping Captain Resistance alive."},{"t":"Taste it, just once.","f":"Mansoul only meant to 'taste' the fruit too. Then the gates opened."},{"t":"Pretend to drink so they leave you alone.","f":"Better than drinking, but a clear, kind 'no' is braver and safer."}]},{"title":"Midnight scrolling","q":"It's 11:30 pm on a school night. You said you'd sleep at 10. You're still scrolling, and the videos are getting worse.","o":[{"t":"Put the phone down, charge it outside your room, and sleep.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Diabolus built a stronghold called Midnight-hold. Don't help him build one in you."},{"t":"Just five more minutes.","f":"Five more minutes usually means fifty."},{"t":"Keep going. Tomorrow is far.","f":"A tired mind is like Lord Understanding with his window walled up."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"mansoul","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 1 of The Holy War in real life."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"🚪 Know your gates. Ears, eyes, mouth: notice what you let in every day: music, videos, gist, games and friends."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"🛡️ Keep Captain Resistance alive. Decide your 'no' before the party, before the phone, before the pressure."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"⏸️ Don't do the ill pause. When something makes you doubt God's goodness or makes wrong look exciting, walk away instead of standing to listen."},{"sc":"walledhouse","n":"💡 Let the light in. Read God's word and talk to wise people, so your understanding can see clearly."},{"sc":"castle","n":"👑 Ask the big question often: who is ruling the castle of my heart right now?"}],"stops":{"hw1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"mansoul","n":"John Bunyan, the man who wrote The Pilgrim's Progress, wrote another great story. This one is about a war. And the war is over a town."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"The town is called {Mansoul}. Say it slowly: Man-Soul. It is a picture of you: your mind, your heart and your choices."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"{Shaddai}, the great King, built Mansoul himself, in the middle of a wide country called {Universe}. Of everything he made there, Mansoul was his favourite."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Around the town stood a strong wall, and in the wall were five gates: {Ear-gate}, {Eye-gate}, Mouth-gate, Nose-gate and Feel-gate."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Can you guess what the five gates stand for? Your five senses. Everything that gets into your heart comes in through a gate: what you hear, see, taste, smell and touch."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Here is the most important thing about those gates. They could never be broken open from the outside. Only the people inside could open them.","b":true},{"sc":"castle","n":"In the very middle of Mansoul stood a castle. The King built it as his own home. It stands for your heart, the place that decides who rules the whole town."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Mansoul had wise leaders. {Lord Understanding} was the {Lord Mayor}. {Mr Conscience} was the {Recorder}: he kept the King's laws and spoke up loudly when anything went wrong."},{"sc":"mansoul","w":"understanding","e":"smile","t":"We have everything we need. Good laws, strong walls, and a King who loves us."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"But far away, someone was watching Mansoul with hungry eyes."},{"sc":"castle","n":"His name was {Diabolus}. Once he had been one of the King's great servants. But he grew proud. He wanted the King's own throne. So he was thrown out of the King's court."},{"sc":"castle","n":"Now he hated the King, and he hated everything the King loved. And the King loved Mansoul."},{"sc":"castle","w":"diabolus","e":"smirk","t":"I cannot break those gates. Very well. I will not break them. I will talk the people into opening them for me."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"That was his whole plan: not force, but {persuasion}. Keep it in mind, because temptation still works the same way today."}],"quote":{"text":"There is in this gallant country of Universe a fair and delicate town, a corporation, called Mansoul.","who":"The storyteller"},"lesson":{"title":"Know your gates","text":"Everything that shapes your heart comes in through a gate: what you listen to, watch, say and touch. Nobody can force those gates open. You are the gatekeeper, so decide early what gets in."},"think":"Which of your 'gates' gets the most traffic every day: your ears (music, gist), your eyes (phone, videos) or your mouth (what you say)? Who decides what comes in?","quiz":[{"q":"What does the town of Mansoul stand for?","o":["A person: their mind, heart and choices","A real city in Africa","A church building","A school"],"why":"Man-Soul is a picture of you."},{"q":"What do the five gates stand for?","o":["The five senses","Five friends","Five rules","Five kings"],"why":"Ear-gate, Eye-gate, Mouth-gate, Nose-gate and Feel-gate: everything gets in through your senses."},{"q":"How could the gates of Mansoul be opened?","o":["Only from the inside","By any strong army","With a magic key","By the wind"],"why":"Nobody could force them. Only the people inside could open them."},{"q":"What does the castle in the middle stand for?","o":["The heart","The stomach","The school","The market"],"why":"The heart decides who rules the whole town."},{"q":"How did Diabolus plan to get into Mansoul?","o":["By talking the people into opening the gates","By breaking down the wall","By climbing over at night","By digging a tunnel"],"why":"Persuasion, not force. That's how temptation works."}]},"hw1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"mansoul","n":"One day Diabolus marched up to Ear-gate with his officers. He didn't come looking like a monster. He came looking friendly."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"He called for the people of Mansoul to come up on the wall and listen. Many came. They were curious."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"On the wall stood {Captain Resistance}, the one soldier who could fight Diabolus. And beside him stood {Lord Innocency}, a good man with nothing to hide."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Then, before anyone was ready, an arrow flew from Diabolus's side. Captain Resistance fell dead."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Think about that. The very first thing temptation does is take out your resistance. If you decide to say no only when the moment comes, it's often too late."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Now Diabolus's speaker stepped forward. His name was {Ill-pause}. A silky voice. A big smile."},{"sc":"mansoul","w":"illpause","e":"smile","t":"Good people of Mansoul! We are not your enemies. We've come to set you free!"},{"sc":"mansoul","w":"illpause","e":"smirk","t":"Your King gave you a law: don't eat the fruit of that one tree. Why? He's keeping the best things from you! Eat it, and your eyes will be opened. You'll be wise, like him."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Do those words sound familiar? They are almost exactly what the serpent said to Eve in the Garden of Eden (Genesis 3:4-5)."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"While Ill-pause was speaking, Lord Innocency suddenly fell down dead too. Something in that smooth speech was poison."},{"sc":"mansoul","w":"townsman","e":"worried","t":"Maybe he's right? Maybe the King IS keeping something good from us?"},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"And there it was: the 'ill pause'. The people stopped to listen when they should have walked away. A question had been planted. Can the King really be trusted?"}],"quote":{"text":"Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour.","who":"1 Peter 5:8","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Don't stop to listen","text":"Diabolus didn't win with swords. He won with a speech, and the first thing he did was take out Captain Resistance. Decide your 'no' before temptation arrives, and don't stand around listening to a voice that makes you doubt God's goodness."},"think":"What are some 'smooth voices' that make wrong things sound fun or smart: in songs, videos or adverts? How can you spot them?","quiz":[{"q":"Which gate did Diabolus come to first?","o":["Ear-gate","Eye-gate","Mouth-gate","Feel-gate"],"why":"He came to talk. Temptation usually starts with what you listen to."},{"q":"Who was killed first by an arrow?","o":["Captain Resistance","Lord Understanding","Mr Conscience","Ill-pause"],"why":"Temptation's first target is your resistance."},{"q":"What was Ill-pause's job?","o":["He was Diabolus's speaker","He was the town guard","He was the King's son","He sold fruit"],"why":"A smooth speaker with a big smile, and poison in his words."},{"q":"Ill-pause's speech sounds like the words of which Bible character?","o":["The serpent in Eden","King David","Moses","Peter"],"why":"\"Your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods\" (Genesis 3:5)."},{"q":"What does the name 'Ill-pause' warn us about?","o":["Stopping to listen to temptation instead of walking away","Taking a rest","Being slow at school","Pausing a video"],"why":"The bad pause is the moment you stop and listen when you should walk away."}]},"hw1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"mansoul","n":"The people of Mansoul looked up at the forbidden tree. They had seen it a hundred times before. But now, after Ill-pause's speech, it looked different."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"It looked good to eat. It looked beautiful. It looked like it would make them wise."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"So they reached out and took the fruit. And they ate it."},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"Then, with their own hands, they opened Ear-gate and Eye-gate, and let Diabolus in. Nobody forced them. They chose."},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"Notice the order: first Ear-gate (what they listened to), then Eye-gate (what they looked at), then their mouths (what they ate). Sin rarely jumps in all at once. It walks in, one gate at a time."},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"Diabolus marched straight to the castle, the heart of the town, and made himself at home."},{"sc":"mansouldark","w":"diabolus","e":"big","t":"People of Mansoul, I am your new king! No more rules. Do whatever you like!"},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"The people cheered. It felt like freedom. They had no idea that they had just handed their town to an enemy."},{"sc":"mansouldark","w":"townsman","e":"big","t":"Long live King Diabolus!"},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"That night, the gates of Mansoul were shut, and Diabolus's soldiers guarded them. The gates that the people opened so easily would not open again so easily."},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"That's the trick of temptation. It promises freedom. But once it's inside, it locks the doors behind it."}],"quote":{"text":"I will set no wicked thing before mine eyes.","who":"Psalm 101:3","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Shut the gate early","text":"Mansoul didn't fall in one big moment. They listened, then they looked, then they took. It is much easier to keep a gate shut than to push an enemy back out. Guard what you listen to and look at, because the heart follows the eyes."},"think":"Why do you think it's easier to say no to something before you've looked at it for a long time? Can you think of an example?","quiz":[{"q":"Which two gates did the people open for Diabolus?","o":["Ear-gate and Eye-gate","Mouth-gate and Nose-gate","Feel-gate and Mouth-gate","All five at once"],"why":"First what they heard, then what they saw."},{"q":"Who opened the gates?","o":["The people of Mansoul themselves","Diabolus's soldiers","The wind","Lord Understanding by mistake"],"why":"Nobody forced them. They chose."},{"q":"Where did Diabolus go once he was inside?","o":["Straight to the castle, the heart","To the market","To the wall","Back home"],"why":"Sin always wants the throne of the heart."},{"q":"What did Diabolus promise the people?","o":["No more rules: do whatever you like","Free food every day","A new school","Gold for everyone"],"why":"It sounded like freedom. It was really a prison."},{"q":"What happened to the gates after Diabolus was inside?","o":["They were shut and guarded by his soldiers","They fell down","They stayed open for ever","They turned to gold"],"why":"Temptation promises freedom, then locks the doors behind it."}]},"hw1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"Now that Diabolus was king, he set about changing Mansoul from the inside. He started with its leaders."},{"sc":"walledhouse","n":"First, Lord Understanding, the Lord Mayor. Diabolus threw him out of his job. Then he built a tall, thick wall right in front of his house, so that no sunlight could reach his windows."},{"sc":"walledhouse","w":"understanding","e":"worried","t":"It's so dark in here. I can hardly see anything clearly any more."},{"sc":"walledhouse","n":"That's what sin does to our understanding. It blocks the light, so wrong things start to look right."},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"Next, Mr Conscience, the Recorder. Diabolus couldn't make him agree, so he tried to drown him out with noise and parties, until the old man was confused and mostly quiet."},{"sc":"mansouldark","w":"conscience","e":"stern","t":"This is wrong! You have turned against the King who made you!"},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"Every now and then, Mr Conscience would suddenly shout like that, and the whole town would shake with fear. Then Diabolus would turn up the music again."},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"Then came {Lord Willbewill}, the strongest lord in Mansoul. He stands for your will: the part of you that chooses."},{"sc":"mansouldark","w":"willbewill","e":"big","t":"Diabolus, I'm your man! Make me captain of the gates, and nothing will get in without your permission."},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"So Diabolus put new rulers in charge. {Mr Lustings}, who wanted whatever he wanted, whenever he wanted it, became Lord Mayor. And {Mr Forget-good} became Recorder."},{"sc":"castle","n":"He smashed the King's picture in the town square and set up his own. And he built three {strongholds} inside the town: the Hold of Defiance, Midnight-hold and Sweet-sin-hold."},{"sc":"castle","n":"Mansoul looked the same from outside. Same walls, same gates, same houses. But a completely different king was in charge."}],"quote":{"text":"And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind.","who":"Romans 12:2","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Who's in charge of you?","text":"Diabolus darkened the mind, silenced the conscience and won over the will. Then wants and forgetfulness took charge. Whatever you keep letting in will start to rule you. Ask often: who is in charge of my choices right now?"},"think":"Lord Understanding's window was walled up so he couldn't see. What things can 'block the light' in a young person's mind and make wrong choices look normal?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Diabolus build in front of Lord Understanding's house?","o":["A tall wall to block the sunlight","A beautiful garden","A market","A school"],"why":"Sin blocks the light, so wrong things start to look right."},{"q":"How did Diabolus deal with Mr Conscience?","o":["He tried to drown him out with noise and parties","He made him Lord Mayor","He sent him on holiday","He gave him a medal"],"why":"But every now and then, Conscience still shouted, and the town shook."},{"q":"What does Lord Willbewill stand for?","o":["The will: the part of you that chooses","Your stomach","Your friends","Your money"],"why":"And he chose to serve Diabolus."},{"q":"Who did Diabolus make the new Lord Mayor?","o":["Mr Lustings","Mr Conscience","Lord Innocency","Captain Resistance"],"why":"Wanting whatever you want, whenever you want it, was now in charge."},{"q":"What was one of the three strongholds Diabolus built?","o":["Sweet-sin-hold","Happy-hold","Prayer-tower","Truth-fort"],"why":"The others were the Hold of Defiance and Midnight-hold."}]}}},"hw2":{"challenge":[{"q":"Who did the King's court hear had betrayed him?","o":["Mansoul","The palace guards","Captain Boanerges","Mr Conscience"],"why":"Mansoul had opened its gates to the enemy."},{"q":"What does the name Boanerges mean?","o":["Sons of thunder","Prince of peace","Man of sorrow","Little lamb"],"why":"Jesus gave this nickname to James and John."},{"q":"Which were the first four captains?","o":["Boanerges, Conviction, Judgment and Execution","Credence, Good-hope, Charity and Patience","Tradition, Wisdom, Invention and Prejudice","Ear, Eye, Mouth and Nose"],"why":"They brought warnings to Mansoul."},{"q":"What does prejudice mean?","o":["Deciding 'no' before you have listened","Loving everyone","Running fast","Telling jokes"],"why":"That's why Mr Prejudice guarded Ear-gate."},{"q":"Who answered the captains rudely from the wall?","o":["Lord Incredulity","Mr Wet-eyes","Captain Credence","Prince Emmanuel"],"why":"He refused to believe."},{"q":"What was Diabolus's breastplate?","o":["A hard heart","A soft heart","A golden heart","A paper heart"],"why":"A hard heart can't feel the truth."},{"q":"Which five captains came with the Prince?","o":["Credence, Good-hope, Charity, Innocent and Patience","Boanerges, Conviction, Judgment, Execution and Prejudice","Tradition, Human-wisdom, Man's-invention, Rage and Fury","Lustings, Forget-good, Incredulity, Ill-pause and Diabolus"],"why":"Faith, hope, love, innocence and patience."},{"q":"What was on Captain Good-hope's flag?","o":["Three golden anchors","Three thunderbolts","A burning furnace","An axe"],"why":"Hope is an anchor for the soul (Hebrews 6:19)."},{"q":"Which flag did the Prince hang out first?","o":["White, for mercy","Black","Red","Green"],"why":"Mercy always came first."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"No man can serve ___ masters.\"","o":["two","three","four","ten"],"why":"Matthew 6:24."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Diabolus asked to keep just one small ___ in Mansoul.","o":["room","car","song","book"],"why":"And the Prince said no. He wants all of you."},"choices":[{"title":"The boring sermon","q":"In church, the pastor starts talking about honesty. You think: \"Not this topic again. I know it already,\" and reach for your phone.","o":[{"t":"Put the phone away and listen for one thing God might be saying to you.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You sent old Mr Prejudice away from Ear-gate."},{"t":"Scroll quietly. You've heard it all before.","f":"That's a deaf soldier at Ear-gate. You might miss exactly what you needed."},{"t":"Listen, but only to find mistakes in what the pastor says.","f":"That's still prejudice: deciding the answer before you hear."}]},{"title":"When Mum corrects you","q":"Your mum tells you that your attitude at the dinner table was rude. You feel your heart get hard immediately.","o":[{"t":"Take a breath, listen, and say sorry if she's right.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! \"To day if ye will hear his voice, harden not your hearts.\""},{"t":"Roll your eyes and walk away.","f":"That's Diabolus's breastplate: a hard heart."},{"t":"Argue back until she gives up.","f":"Winning the argument can mean losing the lesson."}]},{"title":"Just one small thing","q":"You've given your life to Jesus and you're really trying. But there's one habit you keep for yourself: copying homework from a friend's WhatsApp.","o":[{"t":"Bring that habit to God too, and start doing your own homework, even if it's harder.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! No small rooms for Diabolus. All of Mansoul belongs to the Prince."},{"t":"Keep it. It's only small, and everyone does it.","f":"That's exactly what Diabolus said: 'Just let me keep one small room.'"},{"t":"Promise yourself you'll stop next term.","f":"Diabolus loves 'later'. The Prince says 'today'."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"throneglory","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 2 of The Holy War in real life."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"🤴 Remember: Jesus came for you before you came to him. You don't have to be good enough first."},{"sc":"siege","n":"👂 Fire Mr Prejudice. When God speaks through the Bible, a sermon, a parent or a teacher, give it a real listen before you decide."},{"sc":"battle","n":"🔔 When your conscience rings the alarm, don't turn up the music. Listen to it."},{"sc":"camp","n":"🏳️ No half deals. Give Jesus your whole heart: your phone, your friendships, your habits, your secrets."}],"stops":{"hw2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"throneglory","n":"News travels fast. Soon the court of King Shaddai heard what had happened: Mansoul, the King's favourite town, had opened its gates to his enemy."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"Everyone in the court was sad. But nobody was surprised. The King and his Son had seen this coming long before, and they had already made a plan."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"The King had a Son, Prince {Emmanuel}. His name means 'God with us'. He loved Mansoul as much as his Father did."},{"sc":"throneglory","w":"emmanuel","e":"smile","t":"Father, I will go. I will win Mansoul back. Whatever it costs, I will pay it myself."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"Think about that. Mansoul had betrayed the King. They had cheered for his enemy. They hadn't asked for help. And yet the Son volunteered to rescue them."},{"sc":"throneglory","w":"shaddai","e":"smile","t":"Then it is agreed. Mansoul shall be yours, my Son, if you can win it back."},{"sc":"palace","n":"Bunyan is telling the story of the gospel. The Son of God came, not because we were good, but because we were lost and he loved us anyway."},{"sc":"palace","n":"But first, the King sent a message, a warning shot. He would give Mansoul a chance to come back by itself."},{"sc":"armoury","n":"He called four captains, each with ten thousand soldiers: Captain {Boanerges}, {Captain Conviction}, Captain Judgment and Captain Execution."},{"sc":"armoury","n":"Boanerges's flag was black, with three burning thunderbolts. Conviction's flag showed the King's law, wide open, with flames coming out of it."},{"sc":"road","n":"And off they marched to Mansoul. Meanwhile, back in the town, Diabolus heard they were coming and started to panic."}],"quote":{"text":"For God sent not his Son into the world to condemn the world; but that the world through him might be saved.","who":"John 3:17","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"He came first","text":"Mansoul didn't call for help. They had chosen the enemy. But the Prince volunteered to come and rescue them anyway. God doesn't wait for you to be good before he comes for you. He comes because you are loved."},"think":"Why do you think the Prince was willing to rescue a town that had betrayed his Father? What does that tell you about how God sees you?","quiz":[{"q":"Who volunteered to win Mansoul back?","o":["Prince Emmanuel, the King's Son","Lord Willbewill","Captain Resistance","Mr Ill-pause"],"why":"The Son loved Mansoul as much as his Father did."},{"q":"What does the name 'Emmanuel' mean?","o":["God with us","Strong soldier","Great king","Bright light"],"why":"It's a Bible name for Jesus (Matthew 1:23)."},{"q":"Had Mansoul asked for help?","o":["No, they had cheered for the enemy","Yes, every day","Yes, they wrote a letter","Yes, they sent a messenger"],"why":"The Prince came anyway, because he loved them."},{"q":"How many captains did the King send first?","o":["Four","One","Ten","Twelve"],"why":"Boanerges, Conviction, Judgment and Execution."},{"q":"What was on Captain Conviction's flag?","o":["The King's law, open, with flames","A golden lion","A white dove","A loaf of bread"],"why":"Conviction shows us the law we have broken."}]},"hw2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"siege","n":"The four captains set up camp in front of Ear-gate. Their {trumpeters} blew a loud blast. Then Captain Boanerges called out to the town."},{"sc":"siege","w":"boanerges","e":"stern","t":"Mansoul! The King who made you sent us. Come back to him, and he will forgive you. But if you refuse, we must fight."},{"sc":"siege","n":"Now, Diabolus had prepared for this. He had put a special guard at Ear-gate: {Mr Prejudice}, an angry old man."},{"sc":"siege","n":"And under Mr Prejudice, Diabolus put sixty soldiers. They were chosen for one special reason: they were all deaf."},{"sc":"siege","w":"prejudice","e":"frown","t":"Don't listen to them! Whatever they say, the answer is no. We already know it's rubbish."},{"sc":"siege","n":"Do you see the trick? If you have already decided you won't like something, you can't really hear it. That is what prejudice does to your ears."},{"sc":"siege","n":"Then one of Diabolus's lords came up on the wall to answer. His name was {Lord Incredulity}, which means 'refusing to believe'."},{"sc":"siege","w":"incredulity","e":"smirk","t":"Your King? We don't know him any more. We have a new king. Go home, you troublemakers!"},{"sc":"siege","n":"Diabolus had done one more thing. He had taken away the King's armour from the people of Mansoul and given them his own."},{"sc":"armoury","n":"His helmet was called 'I'll be fine, whatever I do.' His breastplate was a hard heart. And his shield was unbelief. With armour like that, nobody can hear anything."},{"sc":"siege","n":"Up on the wall, though, someone was shaking. Old Mr Conscience had heard the trumpet. He knew those captains were telling the truth. But nobody would let him speak."}],"quote":{"text":"To day if ye will hear his voice, harden not your hearts.","who":"Hebrews 3:15","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Don't block your ears","text":"Diabolus put deaf soldiers at Ear-gate, and old Mr Prejudice in charge. Prejudice decides 'no' before it has even listened. When God speaks to you, through his word, a sermon, a parent or your conscience, don't harden your heart. Listen today."},"think":"Have you ever decided you wouldn't like something (a person, a food, a sermon) before you even gave it a chance? What happened?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Captain Boanerges offer Mansoul?","o":["Come back to the King and be forgiven","A bag of gold","A new gate","A party"],"why":"Mercy came first. A fight came only if they refused."},{"q":"Who guarded Ear-gate for Diabolus?","o":["Old Mr Prejudice","Mr Conscience","Captain Credence","Lord Understanding"],"why":"An angry man who decides 'no' before listening."},{"q":"What was special about the sixty soldiers at Ear-gate?","o":["They were all deaf","They were all giants","They were all asleep","They could fly"],"why":"If you can't hear, you can't be persuaded."},{"q":"What does 'incredulity' mean?","o":["Refusing to believe","Being very kind","Being very fast","Loving music"],"why":"Lord Incredulity answered the captains rudely."},{"q":"What was Diabolus's shield called?","o":["Unbelief","Faith","Hope","Truth"],"why":"His helmet was 'I'll be fine, whatever I do', and his breastplate was a hard heart."}]},"hw2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"battle","n":"Mansoul refused. So the battle began."},{"sc":"battle","n":"The King's captains shot their slings at Ear-gate. Each stone was a word of truth, and every time one hit the gate, the whole town shook."},{"sc":"towers","n":"Diabolus's soldiers fired back from the towers. They shouted insults and lies, trying to scare the King's army away."},{"sc":"battle","n":"In the middle of the fighting, three of Mansoul's own captains were captured: Mr Tradition, Mr Human-wisdom and Mr Man's-invention."},{"sc":"battle","n":"They thought they could fight the King's army with old habits, clever ideas and things people had made up. It didn't work. Those things can't save a heart."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Inside the town, some people began to wake up. Mr Conscience started speaking again, louder and louder."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"conscience","e":"stern","t":"Those captains are right! We have broken the King's laws! We must turn back!"},{"sc":"townnight","w":"townsman","e":"worried","t":"Is it true? Is the old Recorder right? I can't sleep."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"But many people stayed stubborn. Lord Willbewill still guarded the gates for Diabolus. Mr Prejudice still kept Ear-gate shut."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"Months passed. The four captains fought bravely, but Ear-gate held. So they wrote to the King: 'We need more help.'"},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"This is important. Conviction and warnings alone can shake a heart. But they cannot win it. For that, the Prince himself would have to come."}],"quote":{"text":"For the weapons of our warfare are not carnal, but mighty through God to the pulling down of strong holds.","who":"2 Corinthians 10:4","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Truth shakes the walls","text":"The King's weapons were words of truth, and they shook Mansoul. Old habits, clever ideas and made-up rules couldn't stand against them. But warnings alone could not win the town. Feeling guilty is a start. Only Jesus himself can actually change a heart."},"think":"Mr Conscience started speaking again during the battle. When does your conscience speak up most clearly? What do you do when it does?","quiz":[{"q":"What were the King's slingstones like?","o":["Words of truth that shook the town","Gold coins","Flowers","Snowballs"],"why":"Every hit made Mansoul tremble."},{"q":"Which three of Mansoul's captains were captured?","o":["Tradition, Human-wisdom and Man's-invention","Faith, Hope and Love","Ear, Eye and Mouth","Thunder, Sorrow and Terror"],"why":"Habits, clever ideas and made-up rules can't save a heart."},{"q":"Who started speaking up again inside the town?","o":["Mr Conscience","Mr Lustings","Lord Incredulity","Mr Prejudice"],"why":"The truth was waking him up."},{"q":"Did the four captains break Ear-gate?","o":["No, it held, so they asked the King for more help","Yes, on the first day","Yes, with a magic word","They gave up and went home"],"why":"Warnings can shake a heart, but only the Prince can win it."},{"q":"What does 2 Corinthians 10:4 say God's weapons can pull down?","o":["Strong holds","Trees","Houses","Mountains"],"why":"God's truth can tear down the strongholds in a heart."}]},"hw2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"camp","n":"When the King read the letter, he sent the best answer possible: his own Son. Prince Emmanuel was coming to Mansoul himself."},{"sc":"camp","n":"With him came five new captains: {Captain Credence} (faith), Captain Good-hope, Captain Charity (love), Captain Innocent and Captain Patience."},{"sc":"camp","n":"Credence's flag showed a lamb and a golden shield. Good-hope's showed three golden anchors. Charity's showed three orphan children held close in a loving arm."},{"sc":"camp","n":"The Prince's army surrounded Mansoul. He set up his slings on two hills: {Mount Gracious} and Mount Justice."},{"sc":"camp","n":"Then the Prince hung out a {white flag}. It meant: 'Mercy is still on offer. Come back to me, and I will forgive you.'"},{"sc":"castle","n":"Diabolus was afraid now. So he tried a new trick: making a deal."},{"sc":"castle","w":"diabolus","e":"smirk","t":"Great Prince, let's be reasonable. I'll give you half of Mansoul. You take half, I keep half."},{"sc":"camp","w":"emmanuel","e":"stern","t":"No. The whole town is mine. My Father gave it to me, and I am paying for it myself. I will not share it with you."},{"sc":"castle","w":"diabolus","e":"worried","t":"Then just let me keep one small room. A little corner. Nobody will even notice."},{"sc":"camp","w":"emmanuel","e":"stern","t":"Not one room. Not one corner. Mansoul is mine, all of it."},{"sc":"castle","n":"Diabolus tried again and again. 'Let me visit sometimes.' 'Let the people keep a few of my old ways.' Each time, the Prince said no."},{"sc":"camp","n":"That's how it is with Jesus. He doesn't want part of your heart, a Sunday corner, while the rest belongs to something else. He wants all of you, because he gave all of himself."}],"quote":{"text":"No man can serve two masters.","who":"Matthew 6:24","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"No half deals","text":"Diabolus offered half of Mansoul, then a small room, then a visit now and then. The Prince refused every deal. Temptation loves to say, 'Just keep one small sin. Nobody will notice.' Jesus wants your whole heart, not a corner of it."},"think":"What might a 'small room' look like in a teenager's life: one habit, one secret, one thing we don't want God to touch?","quiz":[{"q":"Who did the King send when the four captains asked for help?","o":["His own Son, Prince Emmanuel","One more captain","A messenger with a letter","Nobody"],"why":"The best help possible: the Prince himself."},{"q":"What does Captain Credence stand for?","o":["Faith","Anger","Money","Fear"],"why":"Credence means belief or trust."},{"q":"What did the white flag mean?","o":["Mercy is still on offer","The Prince was giving up","Lunch time","The battle was over"],"why":"Even then, the Prince offered forgiveness first."},{"q":"What was Diabolus's first offer?","o":["Half of Mansoul each","All of Mansoul","A bag of gold","To leave for ever"],"why":"And then he asked for just one small room."},{"q":"What was the Prince's answer to every deal?","o":["No: Mansoul is mine, all of it","Yes, that's fair","Maybe later","Let me think about it"],"why":"He wants all of you, because he gave all of himself."}]}}},"hw3":{"challenge":[{"q":"Which flags did the Prince hang out after the white one?","o":["Red, then black","Green, then blue","Gold, then silver","None"],"why":"Time was running out."},{"q":"Which gate was broken first?","o":["Ear-gate","Eye-gate","Feel-gate","Nose-gate"],"why":"Faith comes by hearing (Romans 10:17)."},{"q":"Where were the Prince's captains first based in town?","o":["Mr Conscience's house","The market","The castle","The prison"],"why":"Jesus wakes up our conscience first."},{"q":"What happened to Diabolus?","o":["He was chained and thrown out of Mansoul","He was made Lord Mayor","He became the Prince's friend","He stayed in a small room"],"why":"No small rooms for Diabolus."},{"q":"How did the prisoners come to the Prince?","o":["With ropes around their necks","Riding horses","Singing and dancing","Carrying gold"],"why":"They expected death, and got a pardon."},{"q":"What did the Prince give the pardoned prisoners?","o":["New clothes, jewels and chains of gold","Punishment","A long list of rules","Nothing"],"why":"Complete forgiveness, and more."},{"q":"Who escaped from prison?","o":["Lord Incredulity","Mr Wet-eyes","Mr Knowledge","Lord Understanding"],"why":"Unbelief slipped away."},{"q":"Who became the new Recorder?","o":["Mr Knowledge","Mr Forget-good","Mr Prejudice","Mr Ill-pause"],"why":"Knowing God's truth replaced forgetting it."},{"q":"Who is the Lord Secretary a picture of?","o":["The Holy Spirit","Diabolus","A teacher at school","King David"],"why":"He teaches and lives with God's people."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Create in me a ___ heart, O God.\"","o":["clean","strong","happy","rich"],"why":"Psalm 51:10."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What was the name of the man who carried Mansoul's petition with tears?","o":["Mr Wet-eyes","Mr Dry-bones","Mr Big-mouth","Mr Hard-heart"],"why":"Real sorrow opens the door to mercy."},"choices":[{"title":"After you say sorry","q":"You lied to your dad last week. You confessed and asked God and your dad to forgive you. But today you still feel guilty and dirty.","o":[{"t":"Remember Romans 8:1: you are forgiven. Thank God and move forward.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! The Prince took the ropes off. You don't have to put them back on."},{"t":"Keep punishing yourself until you feel better.","f":"Mansoul didn't earn its pardon. Neither do you. It's a gift."},{"t":"Decide you're just a bad person.","f":"That's Diabolus talking, not the Prince."}]},{"title":"The nice-sounding name","q":"Your friend says, \"It's not stealing, it's just borrowing,\" about taking snacks from the tuck shop without paying.","o":[{"t":"Kindly say, \"Let's call it what it is,\" and don't join in.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You saw through Mr Pitiless calling himself Good-sense."},{"t":"Join in. It's only small.","f":"A Diabolonian with a nice name is still a Diabolonian."},{"t":"Say nothing and take just one.","f":"Mansoul had to judge its sins honestly."}]},{"title":"The habit that keeps coming back","q":"You've decided to stop using bad words. But your friends use them all the time, and they slip out of your mouth too.","o":[{"t":"Ask God for help, tell a friend to hold you accountable, and change what you listen to.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You're putting that Diabolonian on trial, and getting help to guard Mouth-gate."},{"t":"Give up. It's just how you talk.","f":"The Prince gives strength to say a final no."},{"t":"Only stop when adults are around.","f":"That's keeping a Diabolonian hidden in a back room."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"ram","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 3 of The Holy War in real life."},{"sc":"castle","n":"⛓️ Whatever has been bossing your heart, Jesus is stronger. He has already won."},{"sc":"camp","n":"📜 When you're truly sorry, come to Jesus with nothing but your need. He forgives completely."},{"sc":"court","n":"⚖️ Call sin by its real name. Don't let it hide behind a nice-sounding one."},{"sc":"palace","n":"🤍 Wear your white robe. If it gets dirty, go straight back to the Prince to be washed."}],"stops":{"hw3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"camp","n":"Mansoul refused the white flag. So the Prince hung out a red flag, then a black one. Time was running out."},{"sc":"ram","n":"Then the Prince's army brought up their {battering rams}. Boom! Boom! They swung them against Ear-gate again and again."},{"sc":"ram","n":"Old Mr Prejudice and his deaf soldiers did their best to hold the gate. But nothing could stand against the Prince."},{"sc":"ram","n":"With a mighty crash, Ear-gate burst open."},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"The Prince's captains poured in. They marched straight to the house of old Mr Conscience, the Recorder, and set up camp there."},{"sc":"mansouldark","w":"conscience","e":"shock","t":"They have come! The King's soldiers are in my house! What will happen to me now?"},{"sc":"castle","n":"Next, they marched on the castle, the heart of Mansoul, where Diabolus was hiding. They broke the castle gate too."},{"sc":"castle","n":"They found Diabolus cowering inside. The great giant who had bossed everyone around was shaking."},{"sc":"castle","w":"emmanuel","e":"stern","t":"Bind him. Mansoul is not his any more."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"They tied Diabolus in chains and marched him through the streets {in triumph}, so that the whole town could see that he was beaten."},{"sc":"road","n":"Then they threw him out of Mansoul, out into the dry, empty places beyond the walls."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"That's what Jesus did on the cross. He beat the devil openly, in front of everyone. The enemy that ruled us is not in charge any more."}],"quote":{"text":"And having spoiled principalities and powers, he made a shew of them openly, triumphing over them in it.","who":"Colossians 2:15","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"The enemy is beaten","text":"Diabolus seemed so big when he was in charge. But when the Prince came, he was found shaking in the castle and was dragged out in chains. Whatever has been bossing your heart, a fear, a habit, a sin, Jesus is stronger, and he has already won."},"think":"Why do you think the Prince marched Diabolus through the streets so everyone could see? Why would that matter to the people of Mansoul?","quiz":[{"q":"What did the Prince's army use to break Ear-gate?","o":["Battering rams","Fire","A magic key","Ladders"],"why":"Boom! Boom! Then a mighty crash."},{"q":"Whose house did the captains go to first?","o":["Mr Conscience's","Mr Lustings's","Diabolus's","Mr Prejudice's"],"why":"When Jesus comes, he starts by waking up your conscience."},{"q":"Where was Diabolus found?","o":["Shaking in the castle","Fighting at the gate","Asleep in a field","In the market"],"why":"The bully was a coward."},{"q":"What happened to Diabolus?","o":["He was chained, paraded and thrown out","He was made a captain","He ran away free","He became king again"],"why":"Beaten openly, in front of everyone."},{"q":"What does Colossians 2:15 say Jesus did to the powers of evil?","o":["Triumphed over them openly","Made friends with them","Ran from them","Ignored them"],"why":"He won, in front of everyone."}]},"hw3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"prison","n":"Diabolus was gone. But the people of Mansoul were not celebrating. They were terrified."},{"sc":"prison","n":"The Prince had put the leaders who had helped Diabolus in prison: Lord Understanding, Mr Conscience and Lord Willbewill. And everyone knew they deserved to be punished."},{"sc":"prison","w":"understanding","e":"worried","t":"We betrayed the King. We cheered for his enemy. We shot at his soldiers. What can we possibly say?"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"So Mansoul wrote a {petition}, a request for mercy. Who could carry it? They chose a poor man with a broken heart named {Mr Wet-eyes}."},{"sc":"camp","w":"weteyes","e":"worried","t":"Please, great Prince. We have nothing to say for ourselves. We only ask for mercy."},{"sc":"camp","n":"The Prince didn't answer straight away. He told the prisoners to come to his camp themselves."},{"sc":"camp","n":"So they came, dressed in mourning clothes, with ropes around their necks, as if they were walking to their own execution. They knew they deserved it."},{"sc":"camp","n":"Then the trumpets sounded. And the Prince stood up and spoke."},{"sc":"camp","w":"emmanuel","e":"smile","t":"I forgive you. Every one of you. Your crimes are pardoned, all of them."},{"sc":"camp","n":"He took the ropes off their necks. He took away their mourning clothes and gave them beautiful new clothes, and jewels, and chains of gold."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"The prisoners ran home shouting the news. The whole town rang the bells, played music and danced. Mansoul had been forgiven!"},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"That is the gospel. We come with nothing but our need, and Jesus gives us a {pardon} we could never earn."}],"quote":{"text":"There is therefore now no condemnation to them which are in Christ Jesus.","who":"Romans 8:1","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Fully forgiven","text":"Mansoul came with ropes around their necks, expecting death. Instead they got a full pardon, new clothes and gold. That's how God forgives: not just a little, not 'on probation', but completely. If you belong to Jesus, there is no condemnation waiting for you."},"think":"Why do you think the Prince chose a man called Wet-eyes to carry the petition? What does real sorrow look like?","quiz":[{"q":"How did the people of Mansoul feel after Diabolus was gone?","o":["Terrified, because they deserved punishment","Proud","Bored","Angry with the Prince"],"why":"They knew they had betrayed the King."},{"q":"Who carried Mansoul's petition to the Prince?","o":["Mr Wet-eyes","Mr Prejudice","Lord Incredulity","Captain Boanerges"],"why":"A poor man with a broken heart."},{"q":"What were the prisoners wearing when they came to the Prince?","o":["Mourning clothes and ropes around their necks","Party clothes","Armour","Crowns"],"why":"They expected to be executed."},{"q":"What did the Prince do?","o":["Pardoned them all and gave them new clothes","Punished them","Sent them to another town","Ignored them"],"why":"Completely forgiven."},{"q":"What does Romans 8:1 say there is for those in Christ Jesus?","o":["No condemnation","A little condemnation","Lots of rules","Nothing at all"],"why":"No condemnation. None."}]},"hw3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Diabolus was gone, but some of his followers were still hiding in Mansoul. They were called {Diabolonians}."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"They had names like Mr Atheism, Mr Hard-heart, Mr False-peace, Mr No-truth and Mr Pitiless. And of course, Mr Lustings and Mr Forget-good."},{"sc":"court","n":"The Prince said they had to be put on trial. And here's the surprising part: he made the people of Mansoul do the judging themselves."},{"sc":"court","n":"One by one, the Diabolonians stood in court. Each one tried to wriggle out."},{"sc":"court","w":"townsman","e":"worried","t":"Mr Pitiless says his real name is 'Good-sense'. He says he's only being sensible."},{"sc":"court","n":"But the court saw through it. Mr Pitiless was cruel, whatever name he gave himself. Every Diabolonian was found guilty."},{"sc":"court","n":"Then the Prince ordered that the guilty ones must die, and that the people of Mansoul must carry out the sentence with their own hands."},{"sc":"court","n":"Bunyan is talking about sin here. The Bible says that people who belong to Jesus 'have crucified the flesh'. You don't make friends with a sin. You put it to death."},{"sc":"prison","n":"But one Diabolonian escaped from prison before the trial: Lord Incredulity, the one who refused to believe. He ran off to find Diabolus."},{"sc":"prison","n":"Remember his name. He will come back, at the head of an army."}],"quote":{"text":"And they that are Christ's have crucified the flesh with the affections and lusts.","who":"Galatians 5:24","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Don't keep pet sins","text":"Diabolus was gone, but his followers were still hiding in town. Mansoul had to deal with them seriously, not keep them as pets. When Jesus forgives you, he also gives you the strength to say a firm, final no to the habits that used to rule you."},"think":"Mr Pitiless tried to rename himself 'Good-sense'. What sins do people today give nice-sounding names to?","quiz":[{"q":"Who were the Diabolonians?","o":["Diabolus's followers hiding in Mansoul","The Prince's soldiers","Visitors from another town","Farmers"],"why":"They stand for sins and bad habits."},{"q":"Who judged the Diabolonians?","o":["The people of Mansoul themselves","Diabolus","Nobody","A robot"],"why":"We have to take sin seriously ourselves."},{"q":"What name did Mr Pitiless try to use?","o":["Good-sense","Mr Kind","Mr Happy","Captain Brave"],"why":"Sins love to hide behind nice names."},{"q":"Who escaped from prison?","o":["Lord Incredulity","Mr Atheism","Mr Hard-heart","Mr Conscience"],"why":"Unbelief slipped away, and will come back."},{"q":"What does Galatians 5:24 say Christ's people have done to the flesh?","o":["Crucified it","Fed it","Obeyed it","Ignored it"],"why":"A firm, final no to sin."}]},"hw3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Now Mansoul belonged to the Prince. And he moved in."},{"sc":"castle","n":"Prince Emmanuel made the castle, the heart of the town, his own home. The King's picture went back up. Diabolus's picture was smashed."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Then he put good leaders back in charge. Lord Understanding became Lord Mayor again, and the wall in front of his house was knocked down. Light poured in."},{"sc":"mansoul","w":"understanding","e":"big","t":"I can see clearly again! Everything looks different in the light."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"{Mr Knowledge} became the new Recorder. And old Mr Conscience was made a teacher, to remind the town of the King's ways."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"The Prince also gave Mansoul a teacher from his Father's court, the {Lord Secretary}. Bunyan meant the Holy Spirit, who lives with God's people and teaches them."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Even Lord Willbewill changed sides. He became one of the Prince's most loyal captains, guarding the gates."},{"sc":"palace","n":"Then the Prince gave the people of Mansoul white robes."},{"sc":"palace","w":"emmanuel","e":"smile","t":"Wear these as a sign that you are mine. Keep them clean. And if they get dirty, come to me, and I will wash them."},{"sc":"palace","n":"The town had never been so happy. The Prince feasted with them, and the music played late into the night."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"A new heart. A new King. New leaders. White robes. That's what happens when Jesus moves in."}],"quote":{"text":"Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.","who":"Psalm 51:10","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"When Jesus moves in","text":"The Prince didn't just chase Diabolus out. He moved into the castle, let the light back into Understanding's house, put Conscience to work and gave everyone white robes. Jesus doesn't only forgive. He makes you new from the inside."},"think":"Lord Willbewill used to guard the gates for Diabolus. Now he guarded them for the Prince. What would it look like for you to use your strong will for God?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did Prince Emmanuel make his home?","o":["In the castle, the heart","In a tent outside","In the market","Back at his Father's court"],"why":"Jesus moves into the heart."},{"q":"What happened to Lord Understanding's house?","o":["The wall was knocked down and light poured in","It was burned","It was given to Diabolus","It was locked"],"why":"When Jesus comes, the mind can see clearly."},{"q":"Who is the Lord Secretary in the story?","o":["A picture of the Holy Spirit","Diabolus in disguise","Mr Prejudice","A shopkeeper"],"why":"He teaches and lives with God's people."},{"q":"What did Lord Willbewill do?","o":["Became a loyal captain for the Prince","Ran away","Joined Incredulity","Went to sleep"],"why":"A strong will, now used for good."},{"q":"What did the Prince give the people?","o":["White robes","Black capes","Red hats","Swords made of gold"],"why":"A sign that they belonged to him."}]}}},"hw4":{"challenge":[{"q":"What was life like in Mansoul at the start of this chapter?","o":["Happy, strong and safe, with the Prince in the castle","Dark and miserable","Ruled by Diabolus","Empty"],"why":"The danger came when things were going well."},{"q":"Who was Mr Carnal-security's mother?","o":["Mrs Fear-nothing","Mrs Godly-fear","Mrs Wet-eyes","Mrs Prywell"],"why":"And his father was Mr Self-conceit."},{"q":"What did Mr Carnal-security throw?","o":["A huge feast","A stone at the castle","A spear","A meeting to pray"],"why":"And the Prince quietly left during it."},{"q":"Who noticed the Prince was gone?","o":["Mr Godly-fear","Mr Carnal-security","Nobody ever noticed","Diabolus"],"why":"Every town needs a Mr Godly-fear."},{"q":"What did Mansoul do to Mr Carnal-security's house?","o":["Burned it down","Painted it","Made it a church","Gave it to the Prince"],"why":"But that couldn't bring the Prince back."},{"q":"What came upon Mansoul after the Prince left?","o":["A sickness","A festival","Lots of money","Snow"],"why":"Without him, they grew weak."},{"q":"How did the Prince respond to the first petitions?","o":["He didn't answer straight away","He came back at once","He wrote an angry letter","He sent Diabolus"],"why":"He wanted them to learn how much they needed him."},{"q":"Where did the disguised Diabolonians get jobs?","o":["As servants in the leaders' homes","In the army","In the castle kitchen","At the market"],"why":"Sin moves in quietly and tries to look useful."},{"q":"What did Mr Prywell discover?","o":["The traitors' plot and Diabolus's coming army","A hidden treasure","A new gate","The Prince's letter"],"why":"Watchful people protect everyone."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Let him that thinketh he standeth take ___ lest he fall.\"","o":["heed","rest","money","time"],"why":"1 Corinthians 10:12."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What was the real name of 'Harmless-mirth'?","o":["Lasciviousness","Covetousness","Anger","Prejudice"],"why":"Impurity pretending to be innocent fun."},"choices":[{"title":"Holiday mode","q":"Camp meeting was amazing. You prayed every day and felt close to God. Now it's the long holiday, and you haven't opened your Bible in three weeks. \"I'm fine,\" you think.","o":[{"t":"Notice the drift and go back today: a short Bible reading and an honest prayer.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You kicked Mr Carnal-security out before he threw his feast."},{"t":"You're fine. You'll start again when school resumes.","f":"That's exactly what Mansoul thought. And the Prince quietly left the castle."},{"t":"Feel so guilty that you avoid God even more.","f":"Mansoul's answer was to come back with real sorrow, not to hide."}]},{"title":"The friend who's drifting","q":"Your close friend used to come to fellowship with you. Now she always has an excuse, and her new friends are pulling her in a bad direction.","o":[{"t":"Kindly tell her you miss her and you're worried, and pray for her.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You're being a Mr Godly-fear for her, saying the hard thing in love."},{"t":"Say nothing. It's her life.","f":"\"Àgbà kì í wà lọ́jà kí orí ọmọ títún wọ́.\" Real friends speak up."},{"t":"Gossip about her to others.","f":"That doesn't help her, and it opens your Mouth-gate to a Diabolonian."}]},{"title":"Just being passionate","q":"Someone insults your football club online. You feel the anger rising and start typing a long, nasty reply. \"I'm just defending my team!\"","o":[{"t":"Stop. Ask: is this really 'good zeal', or anger in disguise? Delete it.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You pulled the mask off Lord Anger."},{"t":"Send it. They started it.","f":"That's Anger calling himself Good-zeal."},{"t":"Send it, but anonymously.","f":"A disguise on top of a disguise."}]},{"title":"When God seems quiet","q":"You've been praying for months for your dad to find a job. Nothing has happened, and you're thinking of giving up on prayer.","o":[{"t":"Keep praying, tell God honestly how you feel, and ask an adult you trust to pray with you.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! \"Komai nisan dare, gari zai waye.\" Morning will come."},{"t":"Stop praying. It's not working.","f":"Mr Godly-fear said, 'We keep asking.'"},{"t":"Pray, but only when you remember.","f":"Luke 18:1 says always pray, and don't lose heart."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"banquet","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 4 of The Holy War in real life."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"⏰ Watch out after big wins. Keep visiting the Prince every day, even when everything feels fine."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"🧓 Be a Mr Godly-fear. Notice when you or your friends are drifting, and speak up in love."},{"sc":"night","n":"✉️ When God seems quiet, keep praying. Silence is often 'keep coming', not 'no'."},{"sc":"torches","n":"🎭 Pull off the masks. Greed isn't 'being careful', impurity isn't 'harmless fun', and anger isn't always 'good zeal'."}],"stops":{"hw4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"mansoul","n":"For a while, life in Mansoul was wonderful. The Prince lived in the castle. People visited him every day. The town was strong, happy and safe."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"But in Mansoul there lived a man called {Mr Carnal-security}. His father was Mr {Self-conceit}, and his mother was Mrs Fear-nothing."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"With parents like that, you can guess what he was like. He was cheerful, confident and very easy to like."},{"sc":"mansoul","w":"carnal","e":"big","t":"Look at us! Strong walls, brave captains, white robes. Nothing can touch Mansoul now. Relax, my people!"},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Slowly, people started to listen to him. They felt so safe that they stopped visiting the Prince. Why bother? Everything was fine."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Days went by. Then weeks. The road up to the castle grew quiet."},{"sc":"castle","n":"The Prince noticed. He waited for them to come. They didn't."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"One day, Mr Carnal-security threw a huge feast. There was music, laughter and lots of food. Everybody important came."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"carnal","e":"big","t":"Eat, drink and enjoy! We've earned it. We don't need to worry about anything any more!"},{"sc":"castle","n":"And while the party was going on, Prince Emmanuel quietly {withdrew}. He left the castle and went back to his Father's court. Nobody even noticed he had gone."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"That's the danger. Mansoul wasn't attacked. It didn't fall into some big sin. It just got comfortable, and slowly drifted away from the Prince."}],"quote":{"text":"Wherefore let him that thinketh he standeth take heed lest he fall.","who":"1 Corinthians 10:12","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Comfy is dangerous","text":"Mansoul didn't fall because of a big attack. It fell asleep. Feeling 'I'm fine, I don't need to pray or read today' is how hearts drift away from God. The most dangerous moment is often right after a big victory."},"think":"Mr Carnal-security's parents were Self-conceit and Fear-nothing. How can thinking 'I'm strong, I'll be fine' actually make a person weaker?","quiz":[{"q":"Who were Mr Carnal-security's parents?","o":["Mr Self-conceit and Mrs Fear-nothing","Mr Conscience and Mrs Kind","Shaddai and Emmanuel","Mr Prejudice and Mrs Deaf"],"why":"Pride plus carelessness."},{"q":"What did Mr Carnal-security tell Mansoul?","o":["Relax, nothing can touch us now","Run to the Prince","Guard the gates","Pray more"],"why":"It sounded nice. It was dangerous."},{"q":"What did the people stop doing?","o":["Visiting the Prince","Eating","Sleeping","Going to market"],"why":"They felt too safe to need him."},{"q":"What did the Prince do during the feast?","o":["Quietly withdrew to his Father's court","Joined the party","Shouted at everyone","Built a new gate"],"why":"And nobody even noticed."},{"q":"How did Mansoul drift away this time?","o":["By getting too comfortable","By a big attack","By an earthquake","By a flood"],"why":"No battle, just a slow drift."}]},"hw4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"banquet","n":"At the feast, one guest was not laughing. He sat quietly, eating almost nothing. His name was {Mr Godly-fear}."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"carnal","e":"smirk","t":"Mr Godly-fear! Why the long face? Have some more meat! Enjoy yourself!"},{"sc":"banquet","w":"godlyfear","e":"stern","t":"Mr Carnal-security, how can I enjoy myself? Don't you know? The Prince is gone."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"The room went silent. Somebody dropped a cup."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"godlyfear","e":"worried","t":"He left because we stopped coming to him. You told us we were safe, and we believed you. And all this time, the Prince was {grieved}."},{"sc":"castle","n":"Some people ran up to the castle. Godly-fear was right. The Prince's rooms were empty."},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"Mansoul was ashamed and angry. They turned on Mr Carnal-security and burned his house to the ground."},{"sc":"mansouldark","n":"But burning a house couldn't bring the Prince back. Something much deeper had gone wrong."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"Bunyan's name for this old man is wonderful. Godly fear isn't being scared of God. It's taking him so seriously that you don't want to hurt him or drift away from him."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"Every town needs a Mr Godly-fear: someone brave enough to say 'Something is wrong' when everyone else is laughing."}],"quote":{"text":"The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom.","who":"Proverbs 9:10","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Be the one who notices","text":"Everybody at the party was having fun. Only Mr Godly-fear noticed that the Prince was gone. Godly fear means taking God seriously enough to notice when you are drifting, and being brave enough to say so, even when everyone else is laughing."},"think":"Is there anyone in your life who acts like Mr Godly-fear, someone who will tell you the truth when you are drifting? Could you be that person for someone else?","proverb":{"text":"Àgbà kì í wà lọ́jà kí orí ọmọ títún wọ́.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"An elder doesn't stand in the market and let the baby's head flop over. A wise person doesn't watch quietly while things go wrong."},"quiz":[{"q":"Who was not laughing at the feast?","o":["Mr Godly-fear","Mr Carnal-security","Lord Willbewill","Everyone was laughing"],"why":"He knew something was wrong."},{"q":"What did Mr Godly-fear tell the guests?","o":["The Prince is gone","The food is cold","Diabolus is dead","It's time for bed"],"why":"And the room went silent."},{"q":"Why had the Prince left?","o":["The people stopped coming to him","He was tired of Mansoul","Diabolus chased him away","He went on holiday"],"why":"They drifted. He was grieved."},{"q":"What does 'godly fear' mean?","o":["Taking God seriously so you don't drift from him","Being terrified of God","Fearing other people","Being scared of the dark"],"why":"It's love that takes God seriously."},{"q":"What does the Yoruba proverb teach?","o":["A wise person doesn't watch quietly while things go wrong","Babies should stay at home","Markets are dangerous","Elders should rest"],"why":"Like Mr Godly-fear, speak up."}]},"hw4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"townnight","n":"Now Mansoul was frightened. The Prince was gone. And when they went to the {Lord Secretary} for help, he was grieved too, and quiet."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Then a sickness spread through Mansoul. People felt weak and tired. Even the captains could hardly lift their swords."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"godlyfear","e":"stern","t":"We must write to the Prince. We must tell him we are sorry, and beg him to come back."},{"sc":"palace","n":"So they wrote a petition and sent it to the Prince at his Father's court. They waited. No answer."},{"sc":"palace","n":"They wrote another one. They waited. Still no answer."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"townsman","e":"worried","t":"He isn't answering. Maybe he's forgotten us. Maybe we should stop asking."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"godlyfear","e":"stern","t":"No! We keep asking. We hurt him by forgetting him. We won't make it worse by giving up on him."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"So Mansoul kept going. Petition after petition. Day after day. With tears, and with real sorrow."},{"sc":"night","n":"Why didn't the Prince answer straight away? He hadn't stopped loving them. He wanted Mansoul to learn how much they needed him, so they would never drift again."},{"sc":"night","n":"Sometimes God's silence isn't a 'no'. It's a 'keep coming'. Keep praying, even when the answer seems slow."}],"quote":{"text":"Men ought always to pray, and not to faint.","who":"Luke 18:1","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Keep asking","text":"Mansoul's petitions seemed to hit a wall. But Mr Godly-fear said, 'We keep asking.' When God seems quiet, don't give up on him. Sometimes the waiting itself is how he teaches us how much we need him."},"think":"Have you ever prayed for something and felt like no answer came? What helps you keep praying in times like that?","proverb":{"text":"Komai nisan dare, gari zai waye.","lang":"Hausa","mean":"No matter how long the night, morning will come."},"quiz":[{"q":"What spread through Mansoul after the Prince left?","o":["A sickness that made everyone weak","A party","A flood","A new song"],"why":"Without the Prince, Mansoul grew weak."},{"q":"What did Mansoul do to ask the Prince to return?","o":["Wrote petitions to him","Built a statue","Sent a gift of gold","Nothing"],"why":"Petitions are like prayers."},{"q":"What happened when they sent the first petitions?","o":["No answer came","The Prince came at once","Diabolus answered","The letters were lost"],"why":"The answer seemed slow."},{"q":"What did Mr Godly-fear say when people wanted to stop asking?","o":["We keep asking","Let's give up","Let's ask Diabolus","Let's have another feast"],"why":"Don't give up on him."},{"q":"What does Luke 18:1 tell us?","o":["Always pray and do not faint","Pray only on Sundays","Pray only when things are easy","Pray once and stop"],"why":"Keep going, even when it's slow."}]},"hw4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"townnight","n":"Meanwhile, some Diabolonians were still hiding in the dark corners of Mansoul. When they heard the Prince had gone, they got excited."},{"sc":"dungeon","n":"They sent a secret letter to Diabolus: 'The Prince is gone. The town is weak. Come back!' And they made a sneaky plan."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Three of the Diabolonians put on a {disguise} and changed their names. Then they got jobs as servants in the homes of Mansoul's leaders."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Lord {Covetousness} (greed) called himself '{Prudent-thrifty}': careful with money. Who could argue with that?"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Lord {Lasciviousness} (impurity) called himself '{Harmless-mirth}': just innocent fun. What's wrong with a bit of fun?"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"And Lord Anger called himself '{Good-zeal}': keen to do right. Isn't it good to be passionate?"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Do you see how clever that is? Greed pretends to be wisdom. Impurity pretends to be fun. Anger pretends to be standing up for what's right."},{"sc":"night","n":"But there was a man in Mansoul called {Mr Prywell}. He was always watching and listening, and one night he overheard the Diabolonians' plans."},{"sc":"night","w":"prywell","e":"shock","t":"Those new servants aren't who they say they are! They're Diabolus's men, and he's coming back with an army!"},{"sc":"torches","n":"Mansoul searched the town, house by house, with torches. The traitors were found and their disguises pulled off."},{"sc":"torches","n":"But Prywell's news was still true. Outside the walls, Diabolus was gathering a huge army. The hardest battle was still to come."}],"quote":{"text":"Woe unto them that call evil good, and good evil; that put darkness for light, and light for darkness.","who":"Isaiah 5:20","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Pull off the mask","text":"Greed called itself 'careful with money'. Impurity called itself 'harmless fun'. Anger called itself 'good zeal'. Sin rarely shows up with its real name. Be like Mr Prywell: look closely and ask, 'What is this really?'"},"think":"Can you think of a sin that today's world gives a nice-sounding name? What's its real name?","proverb":{"text":"Ilé tí a fi itọ́ mọ, ìrì ni yóò wó o.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"A house built with spit will be knocked down by the dew. Something built on lies won't last."},"quiz":[{"q":"What did Lord Covetousness call himself?","o":["Prudent-thrifty","Harmless-mirth","Good-zeal","Mr Kind"],"why":"Greed pretending to be wisdom."},{"q":"What did Lord Lasciviousness call himself?","o":["Harmless-mirth","Prudent-thrifty","Good-zeal","Mr Brave"],"why":"Impurity pretending to be innocent fun."},{"q":"What did Lord Anger call himself?","o":["Good-zeal","Harmless-mirth","Prudent-thrifty","Mr Calm"],"why":"Anger pretending to be standing up for right."},{"q":"Who discovered the plot?","o":["Mr Prywell","Mr Carnal-security","Diabolus","Mr Lustings"],"why":"He watched and listened closely."},{"q":"What does Isaiah 5:20 warn against?","o":["Calling evil good and good evil","Eating too much","Going out at night","Speaking loudly"],"why":"Don't let sin wear a nice name."}]}}},"hw5":{"challenge":[{"q":"Who led Diabolus's army of Doubters?","o":["Lord Incredulity","Mr Godly-fear","Mr Wet-eyes","Captain Boanerges"],"why":"Unbelief leads doubt."},{"q":"How did the Doubters first attack Mansoul?","o":["With questions and a frightening drum","With water","With gifts","With music and dancing"],"why":"Doubts get into your head."},{"q":"Name a kind of Doubter in Diabolus's army.","o":["Grace-doubters","Bread-doubters","Football-doubters","Rain-doubters"],"why":"Each attacked one of God's promises."},{"q":"Who did the Lord Secretary say should carry the petition?","o":["Captain Credence","Mr Carnal-security","Mr Prejudice","Lord Willbewill"],"why":"Prayers carried by faith."},{"q":"Who received the Prince's letter?","o":["Captain Credence","Diabolus","Lord Incredulity","Mr Lustings"],"why":"Faith receives God's word."},{"q":"Which armour piece does faith become in Ephesians 6?","o":["The shield","The shoes","The belt","The helmet"],"why":"The shield of faith quenches fiery darts."},{"q":"How were the Doubters defeated?","o":["The Prince returned and they were trapped","They got tired and left","Mansoul surrendered","They became friends"],"why":"The Prince kept his promise."},{"q":"Why did the Prince let some Diabolonians remain?","o":["To keep Mansoul watchful","By mistake","To make Mansoul sad","As a punishment"],"why":"So they would keep coming to him."},{"q":"What were the Prince's last words in the book?","o":["Hold fast till I come","Goodbye for ever","You are on your own","Open all the gates"],"why":"The great promise at the end of The Holy War."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"I will never leave thee, nor ___ thee.\"","o":["forsake","forget","follow","find"],"why":"Hebrews 13:5."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! The town of Mansoul is really a picture of what?","o":["Your heart and life","A city in England","A school","A football stadium"],"why":"Guard your gates, and hold fast!"},"choices":[{"title":"The 3 am doubt","q":"You wake up in the night and a thought hits you: \"What if God isn't real? What if I've been fooling myself?\" You feel scared.","o":[{"t":"Tell God honestly, \"Lord, I believe; help my unbelief,\" and talk to a trusted Christian adult tomorrow.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You took your doubt to the right place, and put it into Captain Credence's hand."},{"t":"Hide it. Good Christians aren't supposed to doubt.","f":"Doubts grow in the dark. Bring them into the light."},{"t":"Decide it's all false and stop going to church.","f":"That's opening the gate to Lord Incredulity's army."}]},{"title":"\"You're not really saved\"","q":"You messed up badly at school this week. A voice in your head keeps saying, \"A real Christian wouldn't do that. God's finished with you.\"","o":[{"t":"Confess it to God, remember Romans 8:1 and Hebrews 13:5, and get back up.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You held up the shield of faith against a Salvation-doubter."},{"t":"Believe the voice and give up.","f":"That's the drum beating outside Ear-gate. Don't open the gate."},{"t":"Pretend it never happened.","f":"The Prince said: when you fall, come straight back to me."}]},{"title":"When friends laugh at your faith","q":"Some older students mock you for praying before lunch. \"Your God is a fairy tale,\" one says. Your friends are watching.","o":[{"t":"Stay calm, smile, keep praying, and be kind to them anyway.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You held the line, and kindness is a strong answer."},{"t":"Stop praying in public from now on.","f":"That's handing Ear-gate to the Doubters."},{"t":"Insult them back.","f":"That's Lord Anger in his Good-zeal disguise."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"mansoul","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's how you'll use The Holy War for the rest of your life."},{"sc":"siege","n":"❓ When doubts come, don't hide them and don't open the gate. Take them to God honestly."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"🛡️ Pray with faith. Put your prayers into Captain Credence's hand, and hold up God's promises like a shield."},{"sc":"castle","n":"🤴 Remember: even when you can't feel him, the Prince hasn't forgotten you. He never leaves."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"🏰 Watch your five gates. Keep the Prince in the castle. Keep Mr Conscience and Mr Godly-fear on the job."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"✊ Hold fast till he comes. Well done, Defender of Mansoul!"}],"stops":{"hw5s1":{"story":[{"sc":"battlehill","n":"Diabolus was back. And this time he had brought a huge army, twenty thousand strong."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"Who was the {general} in charge? Lord Incredulity, the one who had escaped from prison. Unbelief was leading the attack."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"His soldiers were called {Doubters}. And each group was trained to attack a different promise of God."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"There were Grace-doubters, Faith-doubters, Salvation-doubters, Perseverance-doubters, Resurrection-doubters and Glory-doubters."},{"sc":"siege","n":"They marched right up to Ear-gate, and Diabolus's {drummer} began to beat his drum. Boom, boom, boom, all night long."},{"sc":"siege","w":"incredulity","e":"smirk","t":"Mansoul! Your Prince has left you. He isn't coming back. You were never really forgiven. Open the gates!"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Inside the town, people couldn't sleep. The drum and the shouting got into their heads."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"townsman","e":"worried","t":"What if they're right? What if the Prince doesn't want us any more?"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Notice something. The Doubters didn't attack with swords first. They attacked with questions. 'Are you sure God loves you? Are you sure you're forgiven?'"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Doubts like that come to every follower of Jesus at some point. Having doubts doesn't make you a bad Christian. What matters is where you take them."},{"sc":"castle","n":"And Mansoul knew exactly where to take them. They didn't open the gates. They kept the gates shut, and went to pray."}],"quote":{"text":"Lord, I believe; help thou mine unbelief.","who":"Mark 9:24","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Take your doubts to God","text":"The Doubters didn't come with swords. They came with questions: 'Are you sure?' Every Christian faces doubts sometimes. Don't open the gates to them, and don't hide them either. Bring them to God honestly, like the father who said, 'Lord, I believe; help my unbelief.'"},"think":"Which 'Doubter' do you think attacks young people the most: 'God doesn't really love you', 'You're not really forgiven', or 'You won't make it to the end'?","quiz":[{"q":"Who was the general of Diabolus's new army?","o":["Lord Incredulity","Mr Godly-fear","Captain Credence","Mr Prejudice"],"why":"The one who escaped from prison: unbelief."},{"q":"What were Diabolus's soldiers called?","o":["Doubters","Believers","Runners","Singers"],"why":"Each attacked a different promise of God."},{"q":"What did the Doubters attack with first?","o":["Questions that made people unsure","Fire","Arrows","Rocks"],"why":"'Are you sure God loves you?'"},{"q":"Does having doubts make you a bad Christian?","o":["No, what matters is where you take them","Yes, always","Only on Sundays","Only if you're old"],"why":"Take them to God."},{"q":"What did Mansoul do instead of opening the gates?","o":["Kept them shut and went to pray","Ran away","Joined the Doubters","Had a feast"],"why":"That's the right place to take doubts."}]},"hw5s2":{"story":[{"sc":"townnight","n":"Mansoul wrote another petition to the Prince. But this time, they asked the Lord Secretary for help first."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"And the Lord Secretary gave them a piece of advice that changed everything."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"'Put your petition into the hand of Captain Credence,' he said. 'Let him carry it to the Prince.'"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Remember who Captain Credence is? Faith. Bunyan is saying that our prayers reach God when they are carried by faith: trusting that he hears and that he is good."},{"sc":"palace","n":"This time, an answer came! A letter from the Prince, addressed to Captain Credence."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"credence","e":"big","t":"Listen, everyone! The Prince says: 'I have not forgotten you. I am coming. Hold on, and fight bravely until I arrive.'"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"The whole town changed. The sickness started to lift. The captains stood up straight. Even the drum outside didn't sound so scary any more."},{"sc":"battle","n":"Then Captain Credence led the captains out to fight the Doubters. It was a long, hard battle. Some were wounded, including Credence himself."},{"sc":"battle","w":"credence","e":"stern","t":"Stand firm! The Prince is coming. Don't give them one inch!"},{"sc":"battle","n":"And the line held. The Doubters couldn't get through Ear-gate. Faith had become Mansoul's shield."}],"quote":{"text":"Above all, taking the shield of faith, wherewith ye shall be able to quench all the fiery darts of the wicked.","who":"Ephesians 6:16","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Faith carries your prayers","text":"Mansoul's petitions finally got an answer when they were put into Captain Credence's hand. Pray trusting that God hears you and is good. And when doubts fly at you like fiery arrows, hold up the shield of faith: what God has promised in his word."},"think":"What is one promise from the Bible you could hold up like a shield the next time a doubt attacks you?","quiz":[{"q":"Whose hand did the Lord Secretary say should carry the petition?","o":["Captain Credence's","Mr Prejudice's","Lord Incredulity's","Mr Carnal-security's"],"why":"Prayers carried by faith."},{"q":"What does Captain Credence stand for?","o":["Faith","Fear","Anger","Greed"],"why":"Credence means trust."},{"q":"What did the Prince's letter say?","o":["I have not forgotten you. I am coming. Hold on.","Go away","Make a deal with Diabolus","Have another feast"],"why":"He hadn't forgotten them."},{"q":"What happened to the town after the letter came?","o":["The sickness lifted and the captains took courage","Everybody went to sleep","The gates fell open","Nothing changed"],"why":"God's word brings courage."},{"q":"What can the shield of faith do, according to Ephesians 6:16?","o":["Quench all the fiery darts of the wicked","Make you rich","Make you invisible","Win football matches"],"why":"Faith puts out the flaming arrows of doubt."}]},"hw5s3":{"story":[{"sc":"battlehill","n":"One morning, as the Doubters were getting ready for another attack, a trumpet sounded from far away."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"The Doubters turned around. Coming over the hill was an army with shining flags. And at the front rode Prince Emmanuel."},{"sc":"battle","w":"emmanuel","e":"stern","t":"Mansoul is mine. Leave it alone!"},{"sc":"battle","n":"The captains of Mansoul rushed out of the gates. The Prince's army attacked from one side, and Mansoul's captains from the other."},{"sc":"battle","n":"The Doubters were trapped in the middle. Their army broke and ran. Diabolus ran too, as fast as he could."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Mansoul went wild with joy. The gates were thrown open, but this time to welcome the right King in."},{"sc":"mansoul","w":"townsman","e":"big","t":"He's back! The Prince is back! He didn't forget us!"},{"sc":"castle","n":"The Prince rode up to the castle, the heart of the town, and moved back in. The people lined the streets, singing."},{"sc":"castle","w":"godlyfear","e":"big","t":"We will never, ever let him go again."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"The Prince had never stopped loving Mansoul. Even when he was away, he was listening, waiting and planning to come back."}],"quote":{"text":"I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.","who":"Hebrews 13:5","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"He keeps his promise","text":"When it looked like the Prince had forgotten Mansoul, he was on his way. God never forgets his people, even when we can't feel him. He promised: 'I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.' And he keeps his promises."},"think":"Have you ever felt that God was far away? How does it help to know that he promised never to leave you?","quiz":[{"q":"What did the Doubters hear from far away?","o":["A trumpet","A drum","A dog barking","Thunder"],"why":"The Prince was coming."},{"q":"Who rode at the front of the shining army?","o":["Prince Emmanuel","Diabolus","Lord Incredulity","Mr Carnal-security"],"why":"He kept his promise."},{"q":"How were the Doubters beaten?","o":["Trapped between the Prince's army and Mansoul's captains","They fell asleep","They got lost","It rained"],"why":"Attacked from both sides."},{"q":"Where did the Prince go when he came back?","o":["Back into the castle, the heart","To a tent outside","Back home at once","To the market"],"why":"He moved back in."},{"q":"What does Hebrews 13:5 promise?","o":["I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee","You will always be rich","You will never have problems","You can do anything"],"why":"God keeps his promises."}]},"hw5s4":{"story":[{"sc":"mansoul","n":"When the celebrations were over, the Prince called all the people of Mansoul together. He had something important to say."},{"sc":"mansoul","w":"emmanuel","e":"smile","t":"O my Mansoul, I love you. I have loved you from the beginning, and I have never stopped."},{"sc":"mansoul","w":"emmanuel","e":"smile","t":"You will not be perfect yet. There are still some Diabolonians hiding in your walls. I have let them stay for a while, to keep you watchful, and to keep you coming to me."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Isn't that honest? Even with the Prince in charge, the fight with sin goes on. But now it's a fight you can win, because he's on your side."},{"sc":"mansoul","w":"emmanuel","e":"smile","t":"So watch. Fight. Pray. Keep your white robes clean. Keep your gates guarded. And when you fall, come straight back to me."},{"sc":"mansoul","w":"emmanuel","e":"big","t":"One day I will come and take Mansoul to my Father's kingdom, where no enemy can ever touch it. Until then, {hold fast} till I come."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"And that is how John Bunyan ends his great story. Not with 'happily ever after' yet, but with a promise, and a job to do."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"Mansoul is your heart. The five gates are yours to guard. Diabolus will still try his tricks: smooth voices, open gates, comfortable feasts, nice-sounding names, and doubts."},{"sc":"mansoul","n":"But the Prince lives in the castle. Captain Credence carries your prayers. Mr Conscience speaks up. Mr Godly-fear keeps you awake."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"So guard your gates. Trust the Prince. And hold fast till he comes."}],"quote":{"text":"Hold fast till I come.","who":"Prince Emmanuel, at the end of The Holy War"},"lesson":{"title":"Hold the line","text":"The Prince doesn't promise an easy life with no more battles. He promises his love, his presence and his return. Your job is to watch, fight, pray and keep coming back to him. Hold fast till he comes."},"think":"Look back at the whole story. Which character do you most want to be like: Mr Conscience, Mr Godly-fear, Mr Prywell, Captain Credence or Mr Wet-eyes? Why?","quiz":[{"q":"What did the Prince say first to Mansoul?","o":["O my Mansoul, I love you","You have failed me","Goodbye","Pay me back"],"why":"Love first."},{"q":"Why did the Prince let some Diabolonians stay hidden for a while?","o":["To keep Mansoul watchful and coming to him","He couldn't find them","He liked them","He forgot"],"why":"The fight goes on, but he is on your side."},{"q":"What four things did the Prince tell Mansoul to do?","o":["Watch, fight, pray and keep your robes clean","Eat, sleep, play and rest","Run, hide, wait and worry","Buy, sell, save and spend"],"why":"And come straight back when you fall."},{"q":"How does The Holy War end?","o":["With a promise: hold fast till I come","With Mansoul destroyed","With Diabolus as king","With everyone asleep"],"why":"A promise and a job to do."},{"q":"What does Revelation 3:11 say to hold fast to, so no one takes it?","o":["Your crown","Your money","Your phone","Your shoes"],"why":"Hold that fast which thou hast."}]}}}});
